The class MultiDatabaseManager is internal, so I cannot subclass it in the test project. I will instead write a test that exercises the public RecoverCheckpoint method and verifies the ILogger.LogInformation call by mocking the ILogger and injecting it via the StoreWrapper's loggerFactory. I will create a minimal StoreWrapper mock and a DatabaseCreatorDelegate that returns a dummy database. I will simulate the TryGetSavedDatabaseIds throwing by creating a derived class inside the test assembly using reflection to override the method. Since subclassing is not possible, I will try to test the logging indirectly by calling RecoverCheckpoint and verifying the logger calls. I will write a test that covers the LogInformation call on line 137 by simulating an exception during RecoverDatabaseCheckpoint call. I will create a minimal fake database and override RecoverDatabaseCheckpoint to throw an exception to trigger the catch block with the LogInformation call. This way I can verify the LogInformation call on line 137.

I will submit a test file that does this. 

